e Álbar Albar[oz] e Álbar Salvadórez
e Martín Muñoz, que en buen punto nació,
e mio sobrino Félez Muñoz;

sentences.l:
and Álbar Albar[oz] and Álbar Salvadórez
and Martín Muñoz, who in good moment was-born,
and my nephew Félez Muñoz;

sentences.t:
comigo irá Mal Anda, que es bien sabidor,
e Galind Garçiez, el bueno d' Aragón;
con estos cúnplansse çiento de los buenos que i son.

sentences.l:
with-me will-go Mal Anda, who is well learned,
and Galind Garçiez, the good-one of Aragón;
with these let-be-made-up a-hundred of the good-men that there are.

sentences.t:
sobre las lorigas armiños e pelliçones,
e que no parescan las armas, bien presos los cordones;
so los mantos las espadas dulçes e tajadores;

sentences.l:
over the hauberks ermines and fur-robes,
and that not may-show the arms, well tied the cords;
under the mantles the swords sweet and cutting;

sentences.t:
Vistió camisa de rançal tan blanca commo el sol,
con oro e con plata todas las presas son,
al puño bien están, ca él se lo mandó;

sentences.l:
He-put-on shirt of linen so white as the sun,
with gold and with silver all the fastenings are,
at-the wrist well they-are, for he to-them it ordered;

sentences.t:
Una cofia sobre los pelos d' un escarín de pro,
con oro es obrada, fecha por razón,
que nol contalassen los pelos al buen Çid Campeador;

sentences.l:
A coif over the hair of a fine-linen of worth,
with gold it-is worked, made for purpose,
that not-him should-pull the hairs to-the good Çid Campeador;

sentences.t:
Con aquestos çiento que adobar mandó,
apriessa cavalga, de San Serván salió;
assí iva mio Cid adobado a lla cort.

sentences.l:
With these hundred that to-make-ready he-ordered,
in-haste he-mounts, from San Serván he-went-out;
thus was-going my Cid equipped to the court.

sentences.t:
Ala puerta de fuera descavalga a sabor;
cuerdamientra entra mio Çid con todos los sos:
el[le] va en medio, elos çiento aderredor.

sentences.l:
At-the door of outside he-dismounts at ease;
wisely enters my Çid with all the his:
he goes in middle, and-the hundred around.

sentences.t:
Essora dixo muchas merçedes el que Valençia gañó:
“se[e]d en vuestro escaño commo rey e señor;
acá posaré con todos aquestos mios.”

sentences.l:
Then said many thanks he who Valençia won:
“sit on your bench as king and lord;
here I-will-sit with all these mine.”

sentences.t:
Catando están a mio Çid quantos ha en la cort,
a la barba que avié luenga e presa con el cordón;
en sos aguisamientos bien semeja varón.

sentences.l:
Gazing are at my Çid as-many-as there-are in the court,
at the beard that he-had long and tied with the cord;
in his array well he-seems a-man.
